  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed eleven projects this Tuesday morning, and seven of them were featured here in the past week. Today's four picks are three first appearances, ==an MCP server that lets AI assistants manage Home Assistant==, Garry Tan's agent memory layer GBrain and an LLM stock-analysis dashboard, plus one earlier pick with a material change: agent-browser, whose ==v0.42.0 adds experimental saved flows==. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held only 11 rows at capture, again short against the 13 to 18 rows of early November. The raw page was checked: it contains exactly eleven listing rows, so the short list is GitHub's, not a parsing gap.",
    "All 11 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and recent releases were checked at about 07:02 UTC for the four picks and for ruvnet/RuView; README files were read at about 07:01:30 UTC (agent-browser at 07:02 UTC). Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Six entries featured in the past seven days were left out without a new primary-sourced reason: anthropics/skills, google-deepmind/mujoco, anthropics/claude-quickstarts and milind-soni/OpenMausBot (all picked 9 November), and meta/astryx and sherlock-project/sherlock (8 November).",
    "One pick is a repeat inside the seven-day window: vercel-labs/agent-browser (picked 6 November), for its v0.42.0 release published at 00:37 UTC on 10 November, after that pick.",
    "ruvnet/RuView was featured on 29 October; its recent tags are automated CI snapshots, and we found no specific primary-sourced change to justify featuring it again, so it was left out.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 3-9 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:01:06 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, binary, plugin, skill or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
