      "stars_total": 48715,
      "stars_period": 916,
      "stars_period_label": "916 stars today",
      "archived": false,
      "metadata_checked_at": "2026-11-10T07:02:00Z",
      "readme_checked_at": "2026-11-10T07:01:58Z",
      "readme_source_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vercel-labs/agent-browser/readme",
      "evidence_urls": [
        "https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser",
        "https://api.github.com/repos/vercel-labs/agent-browser",
        "https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser/releases/tag/v0.42.0"
      ],
      "description": "agent-browser is ==a native Rust CLI that gives an AI agent a browser== it drives one command at a time, reading each page as a compact accessibility snapshot with a ref for every element.",
      "why_interesting": "Repeat from 6 November, for a new release. v0.42.0, published early on 10 November, adds ==experimental saved flows==: record a browser task once, then replay it by trying direct HTTP first, then the same request from the page, then the recorded commands. That can make repeat agent tasks far cheaper than re-browsing. The release also centralises session reuse and fixes Safari and iOS sessions.",
      "caveat": "Saved flows are ==labelled experimental==, and replaying recorded requests can break when a site changes or run against its terms of use. v0.42.0 also raises the minimum to Node 22. An agent with a live browser can act on anything that browser reaches, so keep it on a separate profile. We did not install it."
    },
